        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232948089?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Clarify that browsers can use internally-available information about the devices such as user preference over ideal constraints.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">W3C specs for mediacapture indicates that ideal constraints are not guaranteed and that browsers can use internally-available information about the devices such as user preference over ideal constraints. The specs has been recently adjusted to make it more clear.</p>
<p dir="auto">Link to specs: <a href="https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-main/" rel="nofollow">https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-main/</a></p>
